  "id": "DrugBank_DB00796 - MONDO_5044",
  "verbalization": "Candesartan Cilexetil is associated with Hypertensive Disorder through a chain of indications that target different classes of antihypertensive agents. The drug is known to treat Hypertension, which in turn is linked to Hypertensive Disorder via multiple pathways. These pathways involve medications such as Xipamide, Rilmenidine, and Trimazosin, all of which are used to manage blood pressure and are implicated in the development of Hypertensive Disorder. The shared indication of Hypertension across these pathways suggests a potential mechanism of action that involves the regulation of blood pressure and vascular tone. The evidence supports a relationship where Candesartan Cilexetil may contribute to the pathophysiology of Hypertensive Disorder through its antihypertensive effects, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of antihypertensive drugs in the development of Hypertensive Disorder, emphasizing the importance of targeting blood pressure regulation in the management of this condition.",
